<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on Monday of four-day English county championship matches:</p>
<p>Worcester: Worcestershire v Kent - match drawn. Worcestershire 422 and 174-3 (G.Hick 56, D.Leatherdale 51 not out), Kent 276 and 158-4 (T.Ward 52).</p>
<p>Worcestershire 11 points, Kent 9.</p>
<p>Leeds (Headingley): Yorkshire beat Northamptonshire by 36 runs. Yorkshire 166 and 332, Northamptonshire 286 and 176 (C.White 5-31).</p>
<p>Yorkshire 20 points, Northamptonshire 6.</p>
<p>Colchester: Essex v Leicestershire - match drawn. Essex 533-8 declared, Leicestershire 515-9 (B.Smith 131 not out, I.Sutcliffe 130, D.Millns 55).</p>
<p>Essex 9 points, Leicestershire 7.  </p>
<p>Colwyn Bay: Glamorgan v Nottinghamshire - match drawn.</p>
<p>Nottinghamshire 202 and 239-8 (C.Tolley 73 not out), Glamorgan</p>
<p>353-6 declared (S.James 162).</p>
<p>Glamorgan 11 points, Nottinghamshire 6.</p>
